cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Magnus: neutrino oscillation probabilities via the Magnus expansion"
message: "If you use this software in academic work, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bustamante
    given-names: Mauricio
    email: mbustamante@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/mbustama/Magnus"
url: "https://mbustama.github.io/Magnus/"
abstract: >-
  Neutrino oscillation probabilities computed with the Magnus expansion, for an
  arbitrary number of flavours and any Hamiltonian, time-dependent or not.  Every
  truncation of the series lives in the Lie algebra, so the evolution operator it
  exponentiates is unitary exactly rather than to the accuracy of the truncation.
keywords:
  - neutrino oscillations
  - neutrino physics
  - Magnus expansion
  - matter effects
  - sterile neutrinos
  - non-standard interactions
license: GPL-3.0-only
version: 1.0.0rc1
date-released: "2026-07-31"

# The method this package implements, and the Earth model it ships.  Cited here as well
# as in README.md and docs/source/refs.bib so that a tool reading only this file still
# credits them.
